{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785183929,"nonce":"RfdXjI9YmyT4imPGUzTZXRZOSrI=","message":"**Moved onto the critical path by ADR-0062, and absorbed into cba7165.** Closing here so the work lives in one place.\n\nThis was 'blocked on wanting an access index'. ADR-0062 changes its status rather than its content: the workspace service now holds **Snapshot Farms** (tree-shaped views, keyed by snapshot root) and **Workspace Exports** (per-Attempt writable overlays) as real directories on a bounded disk. Without eviction the service fills its volume and stops — so this is no longer a nice-to-have beside the design, it is load-bearing to it.\n\nThe finding recorded here still stands and is carried over verbatim into cba7165: `list_objects` gives last-**written**, which is the wrong key for immutable content — eviction must be by least-recently-**used**.\n\nNew constraint that did not exist when this was filed: evicting a Farm that a live Export still uses as its lower layer must be impossible, and reaping a leaked Export must also revoke its capability.","files":null}]}